+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+A client may request its own conversation summaries over the authenticated connection; the server takes the user id from the connection and ignores any user id included in the frame ([validated by: answers list_conversations for the authenticated user](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L92)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_conversations",
+  "limit": 10
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                                                     |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                                                          |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | An integer from 1 through 200.                                                  |
+| `before` | object | No       | A cursor with `updatedAt` as an ISO string and `sessionId` as its tie-break id. |
+
+The package entry point exports the incoming and outgoing conversation-list message types and their summary payload types, so typed clients can construct and consume these frames without importing internal modules ([validated by: exports the conversation-list message types from the package entry point](../../src/publicMessages.test.ts#L13)).
+
+The server answers with a `conversation_list` whose summaries contain only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount`; the two times are ISO strings and no conversation content or credentials cross the wire ([validated by: answers list_conversations for the authenticated user](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L92)). The frame is served only when the deployer enables `transport.history`; it is refused with `UNSUPPORTED` otherwise ([validated by: forwards the history opt-in to the WebSocket message handler](../../src/transport/createServer.test.ts#L46)). A store without `listFor`, or one that throws `StoreCannotList`, is also answered with `UNSUPPORTED`, while an ordinary store failure is answered with `SERVER_ERROR` without store detail ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when the store cannot list conversations](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L126)).
+
+A list request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, so it may arrive before an in-flight streaming turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a conversation list before a streaming turn sends stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L761)).
+
+**GDPR.** `conversation_list` carries one authenticated user's conversation metadata and no conversation content. The user id comes from the connection, never from the frame, and `transport.history` is the deployer's decision to make that user's history reachable from a client. The retention bound remains the consumer's through the session store and re-cinq/HALEngine#41. A client that wants a row's content reconnects with its `sessionId`; resume still applies the ownership check before replay ([validated by: reconnects to the id returned by a conversation list and replays that conversation](../../src/transport/sessionResume.test.ts#L349)).
 
